Hi Talea,

We moved the demo from simulated/older runs to real ERA5 + Idalia 2023 and ra=
n a matched-window comparison (20 samples). Summary for tonight:

Method snapshot
- Downloaded ERA5 for Idalia (2023).
- Tracked the storm center using local MSLP minima as a proxy.
- Built anonymized payloads (no absolute dates exposed), forecasting 24/48/72=
h.
- Compared Aurora small vs LLM baseline (DeepSeek-chat).

Idalia 2023 (N=3D20)
- Aurora small
  - Track MAE (km): 347.7 / 815.6 / 1060.9
  - Wind MAE (kt): 20.5 / 21.7 / 18.6
- LLM baseline (DeepSeek-chat)
  - Track MAE (km): 392.4 / 806.3 / 1125.1
  - Wind MAE (kt): 7.6 / 17.4 / 25.6

Takeaway: Aurora is slightly better on track, LLM is better on 24h wind but w=
orse at 72h. Overall roughly a draw at this scale.

Artifacts
- Track + predictions:
  - results/era5_idalia2023/track.jsonl
  - results/era5_idalia2023/aurora_preds_20.jsonl
  - results/era5_idalia2023/llm_preds_20.jsonl
- Metrics + plots attached.

Limitations / next
- N=3D20 still small.
- Track uses ERA5 MSLP minima (proxy).
- Next: scale to 200=E2=80=93500 samples + more storms (e.g., 2024).

If you want me to assemble a short slide for tonight, I can do that quickly.

